window.docContents[127].resolve({"/Judgments-and-domains/Domains/#Core-C______--Judgments-and-domains--Domains":{"contents":"A location  is a natural number. Locations are never reused.\n\nThe values are ,  and . The value  is the result of a call to a function without return value and is never stored.\n\nThe type int has 32 bits in two's complement. The partial operation  returns the integer when it lies in the range and error otherwise.\n\nThe environment  is a finite map from identifiers to locations. The notation  extends , and the most recent binding prevails.\n\nThe store  is a finite map from locations to values. The operation  returns a fresh location  and the store . The operation  removes the locations of  from the domain. Reading or writing outside the domain is error.\n\nThe control result  of a command is  or . A  interrupts sequence, block and loop up to the call that consumes it.\n\nThe result error is not a value of the language. It replaces the result of any dynamic judgment and propagates to the whole program. Its causes are division by zero, int overflow, a location outside , an undeclared variable or function, wrong arity and a missing return in a non void function.\n\nThe typing context  is a finite map from identifiers to types .\n\nThe functions of the program form a finite map from names to declarations. It is fixed during the whole evaluation and stays implicit in the judgments.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Judgments and domains","header":"1.1. Domains","id":"/Judgments-and-domains/Domains/#Core-C______--Judgments-and-domains--Domains"}});